+## Research reading room (`research_lab`)
+
+The western ground floor of the existing Amakawa Research building, entered through its real west door from the works research walk. Canonical island origin (−31, −103.45), one unit = 1.5 metres. The usable shell spans local x−3.95..4 and z−3.35..3.35; a short floor bridge reaches the existing facade at x−4.2. The upper floors and remaining building mass stay intact. Both door leaves rest open and the same shell, shelves and books are visible from outside. The interior windows use the actual island skyline and the same weather-station builder at its canonical coordinates. The room is available through the existing harbour/works paths on day 1, days 2–5 and continuing days; sports boundaries and the other closed works buildings are unchanged. Entering the reading room and returning to Works retain the active objective, including on continuing days; ordinary Works arrivals still receive their usual guidance.
+
+Two physical reference volumes sit on the east display ledge. The player carries one to any of three usable communal-table chairs or the quiet desk beneath the north windows. A fourth communal-table chair belongs to the resident reader. The front browsing table holds an actual reference index that opens the same book choices; bound issues, archive boxes and the return shelf give the archive a separate working area. Warm oak furniture and pale walls distinguish it from the blue upholstery and browsing rug; three task lamps light the working surfaces. Selecting the other volume returns the first to its shelf before taking the second. The open page, selected seat and each volume's optional bookmark survive Continue. Saving a reference retains the identical authored illustration in Papers; it does not acquire or duplicate the physical volume.
